{"author":{"id":"60e8a4f6c4ac173f9427846756ea0ba4ba542d61e99b8bc2fc9c99440a92cf8c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795252264,"nonce":"sDyCL8lGD6sMPASG9iPA8R0q5y0=","title":"Keep the session's treadmill target through the watch grace period","message":"Low priority: with a single treadmill or a pinned one, this doesn't matter.\n\nWhen the watch on the footpod loses its link, the footpod keeps it for that watch for 2 minutes\n(engine::watch::Gate, GRACE_MS). The session doesn't: WatchUnsubscribed arrives first, and\nwatch_unsubscribed clears the target and drops the treadmill link. When the watch comes back,\nthe session re-picks the treadmill with the strongest signal, which at a gym may be a different\none from the run so far.\n\nIdea: keep the target (and maybe the treadmill link) while the gate holds a grace period, and\nclear it once the grace runs out or the watch leaves deliberately. The catch: WatchUnsubscribed\narrives before the disconnect reason is known, so the session has to wait for\nWatchDisconnected (or the gate) to decide.\n\nHost-testable in engine; check on the board with two treadmills.","files":null}]}